---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Frankie Seabrook"
  description="Learn more about Frankie Seabrook - software developer, writer, and technology enthusiast."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Me</h1>
    <p>
      Hello! I'm Frankie Seabrook, a software developer passionate about building
      clean, maintainable software and sharing what I learn along the way.
    </p>
    <p>
      I write about software development, programming best practices, and the
      tools and technologies I use in my day-to-day work. My goal is to create
      content that's practical, well-researched, and genuinely helpful.
    </p>
    <h2>What I Do</h2>
    <p>
      By day, I work as a software engineer, building web applications and
      tackling interesting technical challenges. In my spare time, I enjoy
      exploring new technologies, contributing to open source, and writing
      about my experiences.
    </p>
    <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
    <p>
      Feel free to reach out if you'd like to chat about software development,
      have questions about something I've written, or just want to say hello.
      You can find me on:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/frankieseabrook">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://twitter.com/frankieseabrook">Twitter</a></li>
      <li><a href="mailto:hello@frankieseabrook.com">Email</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h2>About This Site</h2>
    <p>
      This blog is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, a modern
      static site generator that prioritizes performance and developer experience.
      The design is intentionally minimal - I believe great content doesn't need
      flashy presentation.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  article h1 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
